{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Sally and the Job Inquiry"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Importance of a Good Reference"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 15}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Exchange advice and suggestions in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "How to Deal with Problems + Offering Advice and Solutions  "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you want to offer advice or give solutions to a problem, you use modals like <span class=\"italic\">might</span>, <span class=\"italic\">should</span> or <span class=\"italic\">could</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "These modals can go at the beginning of the sentence, or after a clause starting with <span class=\"italic\">\u201cIf ... \u201d</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The modal is followed by a verb in the base form. You do not use \u201cto\u201d. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I would/I'd ... <br/>I wouldn't ... <br/>You could ... <br/>You should ... "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You could take a look at her online portfolio. It is very impressive!"}, {"type": "example", "content": " You should ask her questions about world events."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Conditional Sentences with <span class=\"italic\">If</span> Clauses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use conditional sentences with<span class=\"italic\"> If</span> clauses to talk about real possibilities in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the First Conditional to say it's possible that you will do something. In that condition, something else may, will or will not happen."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The parts of the sentence are divided into two clauses: the <span class=\"italic\">If</span> clause and the <span class=\"italic\">Condition</span> clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The <span class=\"italic\">If</span> clause can go at the start or the end of the sentence.<br/>When the If clause starts a sentence, you separate the two clauses with a comma. When the main clause starts the sentence, you do not use a comma."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">1st Clause</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">2nd Clause</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Meaning</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If you offer her a position as a journalist, \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I am certain that she will prove to be a positive addition to your institution. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's possible you offer her a position. In this condition: she will prove to be a positive addition.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Ms. Weston will take the initiative to identify problems and devise solutions \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"if she has the opportunity. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's possible Ms. Weston has the opportunity. In this condition: she will take the initiative to identify problems and devise solutions.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you offer her a position as a journalist, I am certain that she will prove to be a positive addition to your institution. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Ms. Weston will take the initiative to identify problems and devise solutions if she has the opportunity. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to whom it may concern"}, {"typ